#pragma once

typedef struct { const char *name, *icon, *text; } help_topic_t;
static const help_topic_t HELP_TOPICS[] = {
    {"Getting Around","settings","At first start, choose a name and colours. Tap the folded corner for the care HUD, then Menu. Back returns one screen; footer arrows change pages. Catalogues show six tiles per page, settings four. Grey shop tiles are locked or unaffordable. Checks show the active choice. Hold and drag sliders; keyboard arrows also work on the web."},
    {"Care and Hunting","feed","Feed releases live prey, not an instant meal. Feeding also wakes a sleeping spider so it can hunt. Hold and drag to aim, then release to pounce; the inner aim ring gives a perfect catch. Tap the spider gently to pet it. Clean removes droppings; your spider leaves its own every few minutes while awake and fed. Sleep restores energy. Hunger, mood, energy and hygiene determine how your spider feels."},
    {"Growth and Health","hygiene","Age advances every 30 seconds of active time: 2,880 age ticks make a day. The first molt happens at two days (juvenile), adulthood at five days. Molting has its own animation and ends automatically. Keep hunger and mood above 25 to recover from sickness. RTC time enables offline catch-up on the device."},
    {"Play and Personality","play","Play has eight-round Bug Hunt, Color Match and Quick Tap games, earning XP and Silk while using energy. Your Spider shows temperament, bond and favorites. A favorite is discovered after three positive uses of one treat, three completed games of one kind, or three actual visits to one gift. Favorites stay fixed and give +2 mood. Petting and manual hunts build bond."},
    {"Silk and Daily Tasks","daily_task","Silk buys treats, decor, gifts, backgrounds and borders. Earn it through hunts, minigames, check-ins, tasks and achievements. Menu > Today combines Check In, the daily task and one optional request. Tap ready check-in and task rewards to claim them once; check-in streaks need consecutive days. Request rewards are automatic. You cannot spend more Silk than you have."},
    {"Today: Optional Requests","today","Today offers one optional request: pet or finish a game, plus a hunt, clean or gift visit. It pays 5 Silk automatically, once. Tapping the request row dismisses it without penalty or affecting check-in streaks; there is no submenu. No purchase, overfeeding or spotless cleaning is required. Only manual catches and finished visits count. Without a reliable clock, active play days are labeled separately."},
    {"Diary and Memories","diary","Menu > Diary shows newest memories first: favorites, bond milestones, growth, recovery, new achievements and daily request summaries. Open a memory to Pin or Unpin it. Keep up to eight pinned entries; the diary holds 64, replacing the oldest unpinned memory when full. Existing spiders start a new chapter without invented memories from before this feature. Play-day memories are labeled separately from calendar dates."},
    {"Achievements","achievements","All 20 achievements have a goal you can open from their grid. Each unlock automatically pays 15 XP and 20 Silk once. Old earned badges are not paid again. First Pet is available. First Molt comes naturally at age two days. Collection, care, friendship and daily-streak milestones add more ways to earn rewards."},
    {"Treats and Unlocks","treats","Treats give immediate care boosts and are consumed. Live prey species unlock with levels and differ in nutrition and behaviour. XP increases your level every 50 points; level 5 starts at 200 XP. Catalogue tiles show level requirements, costs and ownership. Buying or applying an owned reusable item does not charge twice."},
    {"Decor and Placement","decor","Slide a new or held preview. Solid makes the spider steer around it; Walk Over crosses above it; Walk Behind passes underneath, and only its top half covers the spider; Climb lets the spider walk up onto the item and stand raised, with a floor shadow. One button cycles supported paths; Back/Front reorder within Floor or Canopy. Done saves; Cancel discards; Put Away keeps it. Decor locks while prey is out or Lock Decor is on."},
    {"Gifts and Appearance","backgrounds","Choose a gift, slide its preview, then press Done. Hold a placed gift to edit directly on the game screen with Put Away, Done and Cancel. Cancel keeps its old position; moving is free. One gift can be placed at a time; its shop preview explains the bonus. Backgrounds and borders buy separately and mix freely. No Border is free. Double-tap to dim the enclosure."},
    {"Music and Display","music","Sound has master volume, mute, ten soundtracks and separate music volume. USB Chimes controls device plug/unplug sounds; master mute silences them too. Display has brightness, rotation, Double-Tap Lights and Dim Enclosure. The gesture starts on; disable it without losing normal taps. Manual dim works with it off. Browser brightness uses your screen; no fake USB sounds."},
    {"Power and Saving","battery","Battery shows charge and runtime. Power Mode has Balanced, Battery Saver and RTC Sleep. Screen Timeout dims the panel when idle. Deep Sleep After is the idle wait before sleeping; only RTC Sleep sleeps automatically, on battery and never on USB. RTC Wake Interval is how often the timer wakes the board: 15 minutes, 1 hour or 6 hours. Deep Sleep Now saves then sleeps; the right button wakes it."},
    {"WiFi and Clock","wifi","Settings > WiFi has Scan, Add Network and Saved Networks. Select an authorized network, enter its password, then use its saved entry to sync the RTC or forget it. The radio disconnects after each job. With no saved credentials there is no boot WiFi. Browser WiFi setup uses local USB, not a simulated radio."},
    {"Firmware Updates","about","Find Firmware Update in Settings > About. GitHub Latest checks the latest stable release and verifies the app and matching artwork. Save a WiFi network first. Keep power connected. OTA completion is not assumed: check status, then reset only after installation succeeds. Art changes or failed transfers may need the USB updater."},
    {"USB and Backups","sd","On the website, export a device backup before updating. Update mode preserves NVS and checks compatible partitions; Full Installation is for new devices or layout migration. Firmware integrity checks remain automatic. BOOT + RESET enters recovery download mode. Browser progress and device saves are separate; keep the original backup."},
    {"SD and Photos","screenshot","Insert supported SD media, then Settings > SD Card to back up or restore the device save. Wait for completed storage status before removing it. Use Photo Album for playfield images; Settings no longer duplicates capture. Browser pet backups use local JSON and photos use IndexedDB, not device SD. Photos need their own backup."},
    {"Automation and Privacy","auto_feed","Auto Feed lets wild prey arrive and the spider hunt unattended. It aims to keep hunger near half full rather than topping the tank up, so care still matters. Auto Clean sweeps droppings but pays no XP and leaves live prey alone, so manual Clean still rewards you. Lock Decor stops placed items being moved. Progress is local: no account, analytics or cloud save."},
    {"Device Buttons","lock","On the board, short-press the left button for volume down, middle to lock or unlock, and right for volume up. Locking does not stop care. Long holds retain hardware functions: BOOT for download mode and power for shutdown. In the browser, M toggles the HUD, and Fullscreen enlarges the playfield without changing game rules."},
    {"Training and Expression","training","Menu > Training teaches Wave, Spin and Bow. Five practices learn a trick; practice costs 2 energy and needs a healthy, awake spider with 20 energy. Rest 30 active seconds between actions; menus pause this rest. Perform learned tricks for fun, not Silk. Friendly idle reactions reflect mood, bond and temperament without changing your spider artwork."},
    {"Calendar and Visitors","calendar","Calendar follows the saved clock: morning stretch, afternoon exploration and evening quiet. Day/night shading is subtle and never forces sleep. Gentle Weather starts off; its six edge particles are decorative, not downloaded forecasts. Seasons use northern calendar quarters. Occasional afternoon visitors pay 3 Silk; each new season offers 10 once. No reliable clock means no invented events."},
    {"Photo Album","album","Photo Album has Take Photo, Storage Status and Photo Storage. Only saved images appear inside Photo Storage: eight SD BMPs on device or eight IndexedDB PNGs in browser. No overwrite. Open a photo > Delete Photo > Confirm Delete to free its slot; Cancel keeps it. Photos need separate backups. Generations is a separate main-menu feature, not part of the photo album. Back remembers your page."},
    {"Optional Generations","generations","An adult may retire only after explicit confirmation in Generations. Three family archive slots keep identity, care, preferences, diary and learned tricks. A new hatchling inherits parent colours. Resume swaps the active and archived spiders; neither is deleted. Habitat, inventory and Silk stay shared. No forced retirement, replacement or death. Cancel changes nothing; back up before changing generations."},
};
#define HELP_TOPIC_COUNT (sizeof HELP_TOPICS / sizeof HELP_TOPICS[0])
